# RocksDB Burst Server Event Handler - Message Flow Diagram

## Overview
This diagram shows the complete message receiving and processing flow for the `RocksDbBasedBurstServerEventHandler` class.

## Flow Components
- 🔵 **Blue (Persistence Operations)**: Database interactions, data retrieval, processing logic
- 🟢 **Green (Incoming Message Flow)**: Message reception, serialization, and storage
- 🟡 **Yellow (Lifecycle Management)**: System initialization, recovery, and shutdown
- 🔴 **Red (Error Handling)**: Warning scenarios and error conditions  
- 🟣 **Brown (Timing Control)**: Sleep/delay operations

## Mermaid Diagram

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    A["🔵 Incoming Message<br/>handle method"] --> B["🔵 persist method"]
    B --> C["🔵 Serialize BurstHandleRequest<br/>message + uri"]
    C --> D["🔵 Store in RocksDB<br/>key: correlationId<br/>value: serialized data"]
    D --> E["🔵 Add key to BlockingQueue"]

    F["🟡 System Initialization<br/>init method"] --> G["🟡 Recovery Process<br/>recover method"]
    G --> H["🟡 Scan RocksDB for<br/>existing messages"]
    H --> I["🟡 Add existing keys to<br/>BlockingQueue"]
    I --> J["🟡 Initialize Worker Threads<br/>messageRemovalWorkers"]

    J --> K["🟢 Worker Thread Loop<br/>readMessageAndSubmitToCore"]
    E --> K

    K --> L["🟢 Take key from<br/>BlockingQueue<br/>blocking operation"]
    L --> M["🟢 Retrieve data from<br/>RocksDB using key"]
    M --> N{"🟢 Data exists?"}

    N -->|Yes| O["🟢 Delete from RocksDB"]
    N -->|No| P["🔴 Log warning<br/>No data available"]

    O --> Q["🟢 Deserialize<br/>BurstHandleRequest"]
    Q --> R{"🟢 Deserialization<br/>successful?"}

    R -->|Yes| S["🟢 Forward to Core Handler<br/>moDrServerEventHandler.handle"]

